=== Estimates/Price Estimates.yml
info:
  name: Price Estimates
  type: http
  seq: 1
  tags:
    - Estimates

http:
  method: GET
  url: "{{baseUrl}}/estimates/price?start_latitude=&start_longitude=&end_latitude=&end_longitude="
  params:
    - name: start_latitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Latitude component of start location.
    - name: start_longitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Longitude component of start location.
    - name: end_latitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Latitude component of end location.
    - name: end_longitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Longitude component of end location.
  auth: inherit

settings:
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: inherit
  followRedirects: true
  maxRedirects: 5
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false

examples:
  - name: 200 Response
    description: An array of price estimates by product
    request:
      url: "{{baseUrl}}/estimates/price?start_latitude=&start_longitude=&end_latitude=&end_longitude="
      method: GET
      params:
        - name: start_latitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Latitude component of start location.
        - name: start_longitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Longitude component of start location.
        - name: end_latitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Latitude component of end location.
        - name: end_longitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Longitude component of end location.
    response:
      status: 200
      statusText: OK
      headers:
        - name: Content-Type
          value: application/json
      body:
        type: json
        data: |-
          [
            {
              "product_id": "",
              "currency_code": "",
              "display_name": "",
              "estimate": "",
              "low_estimate": 0,
              "high_estimate": 0,
              "surge_multiplier": 0
            }
          ]

docs: The Price Estimates endpoint returns an estimated price range for each product offered at a given location. The price estimate is provided as a formatted string with the full price range and the localized currency symbol.<br><br>The response also includes low and high estimates, and the [ISO 4217](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217) currency code for situations requiring currency conversion. When surge is active for a particular product, its surge_multiplier will be greater than 1, but the price estimate already factors in this multiplier.

=== Estimates/Time Estimates.yml
info:
  name: Time Estimates
  type: http
  seq: 2
  tags:
    - Estimates

http:
  method: GET
  url: "{{baseUrl}}/estimates/time?start_latitude=&start_longitude="
  params:
    - name: start_latitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Latitude component of start location.
    - name: start_longitude
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Longitude component of start location.
    - name: customer_uuid
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Unique customer identifier to be used for experience customization.
      disabled: true
    - name: product_id
      value: ""
      type: query
      description: Unique identifier representing a specific product for a given latitude & longitude.
      disabled: true
  auth: inherit

settings:
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: inherit
  followRedirects: true
  maxRedirects: 5
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false

examples:
  - name: 200 Response
    description: An array of products
    request:
      url: "{{baseUrl}}/estimates/time?start_latitude=&start_longitude="
      method: GET
      params:
        - name: start_latitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Latitude component of start location.
        - name: start_longitude
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Longitude component of start location.
        - name: customer_uuid
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Unique customer identifier to be used for experience customization.
          disabled: true
        - name: product_id
          value: ""
          type: query
          description: Unique identifier representing a specific product for a given latitude & longitude.
          disabled: true
    response:
      status: 200
      statusText: OK
      headers:
        - name: Content-Type
          value: application/json
      body:
        type: json
        data: |-
          [
            {
              "product_id": "",
              "description": "",
              "display_name": "",
              "capacity": "",
              "image": ""
            }
          ]

docs: The Time Estimates endpoint returns ETAs for all products offered at a given location, with the responses expressed as integers in seconds. We recommend that this endpoint be called every minute to provide the most accurate, up-to-date ETAs.

